Imported verbatim (no local changes in this commit) from
  https://github.com/canmv-k230/rtsmart @ 2c870c85c3cfdab870bdfd1c2fba0fa7c7f4be5f
    kernel/bsp/maix3/drivers/extdrv/aic8800/          -> aic8800/        (Apache-2.0, see aic8800/LICENSE.Apache-2.0, aic8800/NOTICE)
    kernel/rt-thread/components/drivers/wlan/*.h      -> wlan/           (Apache-2.0)
    kernel/rt-thread/components/drivers/wlan/offload/ -> wlan/offload/   (Apache-2.0; third_party/tinycrypt BSD-3-Clause)
    kernel/bsp/maix3/components/CherryUSB/common/usb_def.h, usb_errno.h -> cherryusb/ (Apache-2.0, see cherryusb/LICENSE)
Not imported: the SDIO transport, the WLAN offload control device and embedded hostapd, the
RT-Thread WLAN management/lwIP layers (replaced by the RTEMS/libbsd shim in ../shim).
Firmware: https://github.com/canmv-k230/aic8800_fw (vendor terms), fetched at build time by
../fetch-firmware.sh, never committed.

Local changes (RTEMS port), all inside #ifdef AICWF_RTEMS (defined in ../shim/rtconfig.h):
  aic8800/aic8800_firmware.c
    - D80 MCU1 units (bit 25 of 0x40500000 clear): set 0x40100020 bit 0 before any upload
      (as the Linux legacy-mcu1 loader does), record chip_mcu_id, and load the legacy
      SDK V3 set from aic8800D80_mcu1/ (shenmintao/aic8800d80, see ../fetch-firmware.sh)
      with the Linux patch configuration (pairs 0xb4=0xf3010000, 0x170=2); the shim's
      "wifi fw auto|sdk5|legacy" overrides the choice (aicwf_d80_fw_mode). Auto picks the
      legacy set for MCU1: the SDK 5.0 fmacfw overruns the MCU1 upload window and its
      runtime never confirms MM_SET_RF_CALIB_REQ.
    - DBG_MEM_BLOCK_WRITE_CFM: a nonzero wstatus is logged, not fatal (Linux never reads
      it; the ROM flags the unaligned last block of the V3 fmacfw).
  aic8800/aic8800_wifi.c, aic8800/aic8800_wifi.h
    - EAPOL frames received on a USB RX worker go to the system work queue (4-deep FIFO)
      before the embedded supplicant/authenticator sees them: its synchronous key and
      control-port commands must not block the worker their confirmations may arrive on.
    - a failed firmware command logs request/CFM IDs and the caller thread; a CFM nobody
      waits for (late, after a timeout) is logged with the receiving thread.
    - every firmware command result goes to aicwf_wifi_command_result() (shim self-heal:
      consecutive failures re-enumerate the stick).
  aic8800/aic8800_usb.c
    - a bulk OUT on the dedicated message endpoint that failed with a STALL (only) is
      followed by CLEAR_FEATURE(ENDPOINT_HALT) and a host toggle reset (Linux
      usb_clear_halt()); a timeout keeps the toggle (cancel as usb_kill_urb()).
    - message bulk OUT timeout AIC8800_WIFI_MSG_OUT_TIMEOUT_MS (shim/rtconfig.h, 15 s as the
      images whose Wi-Fi worked; Linux CMD_TX_TIMEOUT is 5 s).
  aic8800/aic8800_firmware.c
    - firmware block bulk OUT timeout AIC8800_WIFI_MSG_OUT_TIMEOUT_MS.
  aic8800/aic8800_wifi.c (confirmation wait)
    - AIC8800_WIFI_CFM_TIMEOUT_MS (shim/rtconfig.h, 15 s) except MM_RESET/MM_START/
      MM_SET_STACK_START/MM_SET_RF_CALIB, which keep AIC8800_WIFI_COMMAND_TIMEOUT_MS (15 s).
  wlan/offload/wlan_offload_supplicant.c
    - each step after EAPOL 3/4 / group 1/2 (GTK, default key, PTK, IGTK, response TX,
      authorize) logs which one failed and its firmware message ID.
    - upload verify: a file whose size is not a multiple of 4 compares the first word only;
      on mismatch log a register/region dump; for the legacy D80 set a mismatch is a
      warning (the Linux loader never reads uploads back).
